# EC2 Deployment Configuration

Use these values for all remote operations (`scp`, `ssh`, `docker cp`, `docker restart`) against the DAST scanner EC2 instance. **Do not ask the user for these again.**

## Connection

- **Host**: `3.20.180.251`
- **User**: `ubuntu`
- **SSH key**: `C:\Projects\Pen-Test\Acunetix\siba-dast-agentic-poc.pem`
- **Docker container name**: `dast-scanner`
- **Remote app root**: `~/ai-dast-scanner` (mounted into container at `/app`)

## Canonical command templates (PowerShell)

Upload a file:

```powershell
scp -i "C:\Projects\Pen-Test\Acunetix\siba-dast-agentic-poc.pem" <local_path> ubuntu@3.20.180.251:/tmp/
```

Copy into container and restart:

```powershell
ssh -i "C:\Projects\Pen-Test\Acunetix\siba-dast-agentic-poc.pem" ubuntu@3.20.180.251 "docker cp /tmp/<file> dast-scanner:/app/<path> && docker restart dast-scanner"
```

Run the scan-active safety check (required before every deploy per `deployment-protocol.mdc`). The script uses **automation** HTTP Basic Auth (`DAST_AUTH_*` in-container) — end-user platform access is **SSO**, not Basic Auth:

```powershell
scp -i "C:\Projects\Pen-Test\Acunetix\siba-dast-agentic-poc.pem" scripts\check_scan_active.py ubuntu@3.20.180.251:/tmp/
ssh -i "C:\Projects\Pen-Test\Acunetix\siba-dast-agentic-poc.pem" ubuntu@3.20.180.251 "docker cp /tmp/check_scan_active.py dast-scanner:/tmp/ && docker exec dast-scanner python3 /tmp/check_scan_active.py"
```

## Rules
- Always quote the `.pem` path (it contains spaces in the parent chain).
- Never commit the `.pem` file to git.
- The SSH key lives **outside** the repo (`C:\Projects\Pen-Test\Acunetix\`), not inside `POC\`.
